# User-level source of truth: `~/.cursor`

## Canonical locations

- **Rules (runtime)**: `~/.cursor/rules/` (`.mdc` files Cursor loads)
- **Skills**: `~/.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md`
- **Built-in Cursor skills**: `~/.cursor/skills-cursor/` (do not modify)
- **Legacy**: Do **not** treat `~/.claude/Rules` or `~/.claude/skills*` as canonical. Edit under `~/.cursor/`.
- **Claude Code parity**: `ln -s ~/.cursor/skills ~/.claude/skills` if both tools should share skills.

## This repo: `IDE/Rules/`

- Treat **`IDE/Rules/`** as the versioned, review-friendly **catalog** for your personal rules.
- After editing here, **sync to `~/.cursor/rules/`** so agents pick up changes (copy or rsync; keep filenames aligned).
- Remove retired duplicates in `~/.cursor/rules/` when the catalog consolidates them (e.g. drop standalone `test-strategy.mdc` if **common-test-strategy** is the single baseline; drop thin duplicate “persistent developer” rules if **persistent-proactive-developer** is canonical).

## Creating new rules or skills

- New **rules**: add `.mdc` under `IDE/Rules/`, update `00-rules-index.mdc`, sync to `~/.cursor/rules/`.
- New **skills**: create under `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (and mirror under `IDE/Skills/` if you keep a workspace copy).
